{"id":"9a11ac7fb28e6200","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-quasi-equational-class.md","title":"Quasi-Equational Class","display":"df-quasi-equational-class — Quasi-Equational Class","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-quasi-equational-class","aliases":["93-df-quasi-equational-class"],"display":"df-quasi-equational-class — Quasi-Equational Class","depends_on":["[[93-df-quasi-equation]]","[[93-df-algebra]]","[[93-df-similarity-type]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-quasi-equational-class"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-quasi-equational-class</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-quasi-equational-class — Quasi-Equational Class"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1a6af4ddc68cbdc4\" href=\"?note=1a6af4ddc68cbdc4\" title=\"93-df-quasi-equation\">93-df-quasi-equation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6730349967b8ffce\" href=\"?note=6730349967b8ffce\" title=\"93-df-algebra\">93-df-algebra</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" href=\"?note=ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" title=\"93-df-similarity-type\">93-df-similarity-type</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\">\\(\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\)</span> is a similarity type, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X=\\mathrm{Var}_{93}\">\\(X=\\mathrm{Var}_{93}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> is a prospective set of coded quasi-equations.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}\">\\(\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{QEq}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{QEq}_{93}\\)</span> have the signatures fixed in their source definitions.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}\">\\(\\models^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}\\)</span> is the satisfaction relation of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"1a6af4ddc68cbdc4\" href=\"?note=1a6af4ddc68cbdc4\" title=\"93-df-quasi-equation\">93-df-quasi-equation</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{QEqSet}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{QEqSet}_{93}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{QEqClass}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{QEqClass}_{93}\\)</span> are defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}quasi\\text{-}equational\\text{-}class}\\vdash\\mathrm{QEqSet}_{93}(\\Sigma;\\tau,X)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\forall q\\in\\Sigma\\;\\exists E\\;\\exists e\\;\\bigl(q=\\langle E,e\\rangle\\land\\mathrm{QEq}_{93}(E,e;\\tau,X)\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Mod}^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}(\\Sigma)\\coloneqq{}&amp;\\{\\mathbf A:\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\forall q\\in\\Sigma\\;(\\mathbf A\\models^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}q)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}quasi\\text{-}equational\\text{-}class}\\vdash\\mathrm{QEqSet}_{93}(\\Sigma;\\tau,X)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\forall q\\in\\Sigma\\;\\exists E\\;\\exists e\\;\\bigl(q=\\langle E,e\\rangle\\land\\mathrm{QEq}_{93}(E,e;\\tau,X)\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Mod}^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}(\\Sigma)\\coloneqq{}&amp;\\{\\mathbf A:\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\forall q\\in\\Sigma\\;(\\mathbf A\\models^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,X}q)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}quasi\\text{-}equational\\text{-}class}\\vdash\\mathrm{QEqClass}_{93}(\\mathcal K,\\tau)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\Bigl[\n\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\exists\\Sigma\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{QEqSet}_{93}(\\Sigma;\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\n\\land\\mathcal K=\\operatorname{Mod}^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93}}(\\Sigma)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}quasi\\text{-}equational\\text{-}class}\\vdash\\mathrm{QEqClass}_{93}(\\mathcal K,\\tau)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\Bigl[\n\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\exists\\Sigma\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{QEqSet}_{93}(\\Sigma;\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93})\n\\land\\mathcal K=\\operatorname{Mod}^{\\mathrm q}_{\\tau,\\mathrm{Var}_{93}}(\\Sigma)\\bigr)\\Bigr]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every member of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> must decode as a well-formed quasi-equation in the same complete similarity type; its model class is therefore typed before the class predicate is applied.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-quasi-equation","status":"resolved","id":"1a6af4ddc68cbdc4","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-quasi-equation]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebra"